// ADR-0076 (#817) Phase 3: a needing function's body defines a closure
// LITERAL that itself performs the effect being migrated.
//
// edp_has_unsafe_construct's `EFn` case was unconditionally unsafe:
// defining ANY closure ANYWHERE in a needing function's body disqualified
// the entire migration, regardless of what the closure's own body
// contained. It now recurses into the closure's body with the exact same
// check instead -- sound for the same structural reason as everywhere
// else in this function: if the closure's body contains nothing this
// pass doesn't already know how to classify, whatever the closure
// eventually does when invoked is exactly as well-understood as any
// other code this pass already rewrites. A `perform ename::Op` found
// inside IS rewritten (edp_rewrite_needing_body/edp_rewrite_handle_body
// gained a matching `EFn` case), resolving through the closure's
// LEXICALLY CAPTURED `dict_pname` -- an ordinary captured variable
// reference, ordinary closure-capture semantics, nothing effect-
// handling-specific about it.
//
// IMPORTANT SCOPE NOTE this fixture exists to pin: this relaxation makes
// the closure's DEFINITION safe to look inside, but does NOT make CALLING
// an arbitrary local closure (`f()` where `f` is a local variable, not a
// top-level function name) safe -- that's a separate restriction in the
// ECall case's `else => true` fallback, unrelated to and unaddressed by
// this change (recognizing local-variable callees would need real scope
// tracking this AST-level pass doesn't have, and risks name-shadowing
// false-safety if done naively by string match). So the closure defined
// here (`never_called`) is deliberately never invoked -- it exists only
// to pin that DEFINING an effectful closure no longer blocks migration,
// and that the rewrite of its body produces valid, correct wasm even
// though the closure itself is unreachable at runtime.
//
// Verified (via a temporary migration-plan probe during development)
// that `Ask` genuinely migrates both here and for a strictly simpler
// case (a closure whose body doesn't reference the effect at all).
//
//   a == 5 (perform Ask::Get, resolved via the evidence dict)
//   main() == a + 1 == 6
effect Ask {
  Get -> Int
}

let ask_helper = () -> Int with Ask {
  let never_called = () -> Int { perform Ask::Get }
  let a = perform Ask::Get
  a + 1
}

export let main = () -> Int {
  handle {
    ask_helper()
  } with Ask {
    Get => resume(5)
  }
}

// #1571: the expectation lives here, checked by `inspect` and updatable
// with `vibe test --update`, instead of in a `__DATA__` tail the gate has
// to `sed` off and compare in shell.
test "effect handle call evidence closure literal" {
  inspect(main(), "6")
}
